WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.100
Speaker 1: There is a super interesting article
in The New York Times about Tucker Carlson

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.690
and journalists and anonymous sources that
I want to look at with you today.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.680
And what's most interesting, there's a few
things that are interesting about this article.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.720
One are the things we learn about Tucker Carlson
specifically, but also what we learn about

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.089
this relationship in terms of trading for
access that exists in general, in politics,

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:27.989
but also in the political media space.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:29.559
So let's jump right into it.

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:34.760
The article in The New York Times called Tucker
Carlson calls journalists animals.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.789
He's also their best source.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:41.850
And the article by Ben Smith starts last month.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.000
I texted Tucker Carlson to ask him a question
that was on my mind.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.859
Did you get vaccinated?

00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:50.410
When was the last time you had sex with your
wife and in what position?

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.999
He replied, We can trade intimate details.

00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:58.589
Then we argued back and forth about vaccines,
and he ended the conversation with a friendly

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:00.840
invitation to return to his show.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.250
Always a good time.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.420
One question you may be asking if you're a
New York Times reader is why are you exchanging

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.979
texts with Tucker Carlson, the Fox News host
who recently described the media at large

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:14.060
as cringing animals who are not worthy of
respect?

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.479
And if you're a Tucker Carlson viewer, you
may also be asking, how can the guy who tells

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:22.020
you every night that the media is lying be
texting with the enemy?

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.350
The answer is one of Washington's open secrets.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.070
Mr. Carlson, a proud traitor to the elite
political class, spends his time when he's

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.670
not denouncing the liberal media trading gossip
with them.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:38.299
He's the go to guy for sometimes unflattering
stories about Donald Trump and for coverage

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:42.970
of the internal politics of Fox News, not
to mention stories about Carlson himself.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.870
I won't talk here about any off the record
conversations they may have had with him.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:52.770
But 16 other journalists, none from the Times,
told me on background that he has been, as

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:57.659
three of them put it, a great source in Trump's
Washington.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:01.509
Tucker Carlson is a primary super secret source.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:05.530
The media writer and Trump chronicler Michael
Wolff writes in his forthcoming collection

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:11.630
of essays, he explained, I know this because
I know what he has told me and I can track

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:17.820
his exquisite too good not to be true gossip
through unsourced reports and as it often

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.850
emerges into the accepted wisdom.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.240
So take away no one is.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.270
We knew it.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.170
But this is confirmation.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.750
Tucker Carlson plays a character on his program.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.280
In the midst of all the anti vaccine stuff,
he's almost certainly been vaccinated, as

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:38.790
has his family, I'm sure in the midst of all
of his attacks on the media and his sort of

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.320
kowtowing to this populist stuff that he does.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:49.590
He is a sort of regular elite insider that
communicates with all these very same people.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.590
Shouldn't surprise us.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.360
We already suspected that article goes on
to say Mr. Carlson was particularly well positioned

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.640
to be a source about the Trump administration,
his Fox platform, where in May he had a nightly

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.230
average of three million viewers, made him
someone who mattered to Trump, a close follower

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.400
of television ratings.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.840
He has a former reporter's eye for detail
and anecdote, and his observations can be

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:17.730
detected in the lurid details of Trump's chaotic
court and Fox's own tumultuous internal politics.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:23.220
Upcoming book by the reporter Michael Bender
includes a moment in which Carlson sends Trump's

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:29.020
calls to voicemail after the first presidential
debate last fall, when he was criticized for

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.920
repeatedly interrupting Joe Biden when Trump
finally reaches.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:38.180
The book describes verbatim an exchange between
the two men that cast Mr. Carlson in a flattering

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.180
light.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.250
Everyone says, I did a good job, Trump tells
Carlson.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.950
I don't know who told you that was good.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.790
Mr. Carlson says it was not good.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.780
Mr. Bender declined to comment on the sourcing
that allowed him to so precisely reconstruct

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.370
the conversation between the two men.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:56.100
Of course, the belief would be, well, the
source is Tucker himself.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.180
The article continues.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.800
Brian Stelter, the host of the CNN show Reliable
Sources, told me, quote, You can see Tucker's

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.270
fingerprints all over the hardcover edition
of his 20/20 book Hoax, which excoriates Fox

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.340
for amplifying Trump's falsehoods.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.260
He said he couldn't stomach talking to Carlson,
who has grown ever more hard line for the

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.620
updated paperback version that was just released.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.740
Carlson was born to a world of insiders and
story shapers and makes no secret of it.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.520
His father was a reporter in L.A. and San
Diego before Reagan appointed him director

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.090
of Voice of America.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.419
And the son grew up with a generation of elite
Washington journalists in twenty eighteen.

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:36.900
Tucker said, I've always lived around people
who were wielding authority around the ruling

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.430
class.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:45.120
A former New York Observer media writer, Shridhar
Papou, recalled to me that when he first traveled

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.919
to Washington to cover the White House Correspondents
Association dinner in the 2000s, it was Carlson

00:04:49.919 --> 00:04:53.219
who asked him, Do you have an invitation to
Tami's?

00:04:53.219 --> 00:05:00.199
Referring to the annual brunch for media insiders
cohosted by Tammy Haddad, the well-connected.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.130
Former MSNBC producer.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:08.729
So here you start to get the sense that not
only is Tucker not the guy waging war on the

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:15.509
so-called elite media, he's actually a guy
trading on his membership in that very group

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:17.050
in his private life.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.050
Surprising?

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.050
Not at all.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.050
Not at all.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.919
A couple other interesting things here.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:26.430
Carlson said he turned against his fellow
elites after the 2008 financial crisis.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.009
His political shift also transformed his long
journeyman's career as a writer, magazine

00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:36.669
writer and MSNBC conservative and make them
Fox's leading tribune of the pro Trump masses.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:41.629
But his decades of Washington relationships
have produced the tiresome conversation among

00:05:41.629 --> 00:05:46.139
Carlson's old friends about what he really
stands for, whether he's really a racist or

00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:48.629
whether he cynically plays one on TV, who
knows?

00:05:48.629 --> 00:05:50.560
And what does it matter anyway?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:55.539
That's the same analysis of Trump when we've
said, oh, it sort of seems like Trump plays

00:05:55.539 --> 00:05:57.160
coy with anti-Semitic stuff.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.650
But his daughter converted to Judaism.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.449
His grandkids are Jewish, his son in law,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:04.419
What you have to remember is that it doesn't
actually matter.

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:11.349
In the end, if Trump placates and coalesces
that very group, it doesn't really matter

00:06:11.349 --> 00:06:12.530
what's in his head.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:16.159
And that is amplified with Tucker Carlson
as well.

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:21.800
And the article points out, as we have, Karlsson's
recent fixations include suggesting the January

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:27.180
6th capital insurrection was a provocation
staged by the FBI and that making children

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.569
wear masks is abuse.

00:06:29.569 --> 00:06:32.490
Do we know whether that is really Tucker's
view or not?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.490
No, we don't.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.789
I suspect it's not.

00:06:35.789 --> 00:06:39.379
But that is something that will remain a question.

00:06:39.379 --> 00:06:43.169
So the takeaways are Tucker's just like all
of these other people.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:44.259
There's really no difference.

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:47.699
He is the very same type of elite that he
decries.

00:06:47.699 --> 00:06:51.740
And unfortunately and I don't want to make
this a bigger thing about populism and grifting

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:59.372
in general, but there is a lot of populist
rhetoric that is rhetoric alone, and it is

00:06:59.372 --> 00:07:02.091
not actually the beliefs of the individuals
behind it.

00:07:02.091 --> 00:07:05.009
And that can apply on the left and the right
on the right.

00:07:05.009 --> 00:07:11.249
A lot of the populist rhetoric is a cover
for just the sort of like elite typical dude

00:07:11.249 --> 00:07:13.250
like Tucker on the left.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:18.469
Sometimes the populist rhetoric is cover for
an authoritarian tendency, which we've also

00:07:18.469 --> 00:07:20.180
talked about before.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:25.719
Last thing you know, you might remember Donald
Trump's discussions of anonymous sources,

00:07:25.719 --> 00:07:31.900
anonymous sources shouldn't be allowed, Trump
even seemingly misunderstanding that an anonymous

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.029
source isn't anonymous to the journalist.

00:07:35.029 --> 00:07:39.439
It's typically that the journalist is just
saying, I won't identify you.

00:07:39.439 --> 00:07:46.650
It's very interesting that such a notable
figure on the right is such a prominent anonymous

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:52.319
source when he's supposedly part of a movement
that decries the status quo of the media,

00:07:52.319 --> 00:07:57.539
which, as fomented by Donald Trump during
his presidency, includes the criticism of

00:07:57.539 --> 00:07:59.099
the use of anonymous sources.

00:07:59.099 --> 00:08:02.850
So nothing massively surprising in the article.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:08.839
It confirms a lot of things we suspected,
but very interesting in that our suspicions

00:08:08.839 --> 00:09:33.910
seem to have been very much accurate about
Tucker Carlson.

